
### 8.2 S3-compatible store (`STORAGE_DRIVER=s3`)

Backup is a property of the bucket, not of the application. Enable
versioning and lifecycle rules on the bucket; the application does not
version objects itself. Server-side encryption is a bucket policy.

### 8.3 What to back up

| Data                       | Where                                | Frequency |
|----------------------------|--------------------------------------|-----------|
| Postgres schema + rows     | `pg_dump` or continuous WAL archiving | Daily full, continuous incremental |
| Object store contents      | `STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT` or the S3 bucket | Daily full |
| Environment file / secrets | The operator's secret store           | On change |
| TLS certificate            | The operator's certificate store      | Before expiry |

The application is designed to be recoverable from these three. There is
no hidden state: the schema is the only structured store and the object
store is the only blob store.

